Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:18:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 166/173] fix(gastown): stop the deacon patrol prescribing from
 one-shot readings (gcp-di7v)

Two deacon-patrol steps turned a point-in-time reading into a confident order,
and both orders were destructive on a store holding every seat's bead history.

queue-starvation-check called any assignee with no ACTIVE session "orphaned
work". A deliberately parked named seat (suspended, on_demand) has no active
session by design, so the line read as an orphan report for exactly the seat
the witness's recover-orphaned-beads step already skips. The deacon's own
boundary list says orphan recovery is the rig witness's job, so the step now
says it classifies nothing and nudges, mails and prescribes nothing about an
unmatched assignee. The code fence is untouched: the inference gate pins
`gc session list --state active`.

Step 3b nudged the mayor to "Raise dolt.auto-push-timeout in <rig>'s
config.yaml" from a FROZEN reading that often clears before the nudge is read,
and the file it names carries a warning about an automated rewrite that
pointed every worktree at the wrong dolt server. The nudge now reports what was
observed, stamps OBSERVED_AT when the detector ran, and orders a re-run of
dolt-push-state-check.sh --json, acting only if the scope still reads FROZEN.
The once-per-condition dedupe marker is unchanged. The block is fenced with
frozen-report sentinels so the new test can extract and execute it.

Validation: gastown/tests/test_deacon_patrol_reminders.sh extracts the shipped
step text and block and runs the block against a stub gc (three tests: no
"orphaned" wording, observation time plus re-measure in the nudge, one nudge
per condition across two runs).

Out of scope, per the bead: the push-direction reminder (no pack text behind
it), the Step 3 STALE wording, the witness formula, and gc's nudge transport.
